metacircular-univalent-unison-of-cubically-receptive-stateboxes-lines-4 = cons "## Reading the name" (cons "" (cons "The phrase is one type, read from its head noun outward. The head is *unison*: many things sounding together as one. What sound together are *stateboxes*: processes, each a condition held in a vessel and changed by firing. Each statebox is *receptive*, and *cubically* so: what it receives is a cube with a face missing, and receiving is filling that face. The unison is *univalent*: two stateboxes whose behaviors are equivalent are the same statebox, and the equivalence is kept as a path along which everything about one carries to the other. And the whole is *metacircular*: the system that holds this unison is itself one of its stateboxes, defined in its own language and checked by itself. Each word imports a lineage of thought that ran for decades, and each word needs the others. Read together they state the work: the language, the product, the knowledge graph, the workflow, and the collective intelligence they serve." (cons "" nil)))
